{
  "dom_id": "step-q115478",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "In an inverse variation, $y=\\frac{1}{4}$ when $x=2.$ Find an equation that relates $x$ and $y.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nNext, we use the given data $y=\\frac{1}{4}$ when $x=2$ to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{k}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2 & =k \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our inverse variation equation is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2x}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
